{"occurrence_no":"1188009","record_type":"occ","collection_no":"151252","identified_name":"Eleutherornis cotei","identified_rank":"species","identified_no":"285528","accepted_name":"Eleutherornis cotei","accepted_rank":"species","accepted_no":"285527","early_interval":"Lutetian","max_ma":48.07,"min_ma":41.03,"reference_no":"49420","lng":"4.750000","lat":"45.866669","cc":"FR","state":"Rhone","latlng_basis":"based on nearby landmark","latlng_precision":"minutes","geogcomments":"\"The locality no longer exists. It was located in a western extension of the Mont d’Or lyonnais, a small limestone mount located 10 km north-northwest of Lyon, central eastern France (‘‘département’’, or administrative region, of Rhône). The fossils were recovered from a fissure-fill situated close to the\r\nhamlet of La Clôtre, near the village of Lissieu. The enclosing rocks, and therefore the fissure disappeared (mined out) by the end of the nineteenth century.\" - Rage and Auge (2010)","environment":"fissure fill","primary_reference":"D. Angst, E. Buffetaut, and C. Lecuyer, R. Amiot. 2013. ‘‘Terror Birds’’ (Phorusrhacidae) from the Eocene of Europe Imply Trans-Tethys Dispersal. PLoS One 8(11):e80357","phylum":"Chordata","phylum_no":"33815","class":"Aves","class_no":"36616","order":"Gruiformes","order_no":"39454","family":"Phorusrhacidae","family_no":"39461","genus":"Eleutherornis","genus_no":"39498"},
