{"occurrence_no":"1226531","record_type":"occ","collection_no":"161187","identified_name":"Gallomesovelia grioti n. gen. n. sp.","identified_rank":"species","accepted_name":"Gallomesovelia grioti","accepted_rank":"species","accepted_no":"304536","early_interval":"Late Kimmeridgian","max_ma":152.21,"min_ma":149.2,"reference_no":"52512","lng":"5.775600","lat":"45.990601","cc":"FR","latlng_basis":"stated in text","latlng_precision":"4","altitude_value":"597","altitude_unit":"meters","geogscale":"outcrop","geogcomments":"The fossils were collected in the small valley of the river Dorches (a river Rhône tributary), situated on the territory of the Corbonod village, northwest of Orbagnoux mine (Long. 5 46' 32.2\"E, Lat. 45 59' 26.3\"N, alt. 597 m). The highly bituminous black shales inside of the Orbagnoux mine (Chateauneuf et al., 1982) contain few macrofossils (A Nel, pers. obs., 2012): mainly rather poorly preserved ammonites and bivalves, foraminifers and ostracods. On the contrary, fossil plants, fishes and crustaceans are known in other layers outside of the mine.","environment":"lagoonal/restricted shallow subtidal","primary_reference":"A. Nel, P. Nel, and R. Krieg-Jacquier, J. M. Pouillon, R. Garrouste. 2014. Exceptionally preserved insect fossils in the Late Jurassic lagoon of Orbagnoux (Rhône Valley, France). PeerJ 2(e510):1-16","phylum":"Arthropoda","phylum_no":"18891","class":"Insecta","class_no":"56637","order":"Hemiptera","order_no":"94230","family":"Mesoveliidae","family_no":"193104","genus":"Gallomesovelia","genus_no":"304535"},
