{"occurrence_no":"1248845","record_type":"occ","collection_no":"164829","identified_name":"Montceaupterum baillyi n. gen. n. sp.","identified_rank":"species","accepted_name":"Montceaupterum baillyi","accepted_rank":"species","accepted_no":"311425","early_interval":"Stephanian B","max_ma":301.4,"min_ma":300.9,"reference_no":"53862","lng":"4.375000","lat":"46.689999","cc":"FR","latlng_basis":"estimated from map","latlng_precision":"2","geogscale":"outcrop","geogcomments":"The fossil was found in the Saint Louis quarry situated tothe north, northwest of Montceau-les-Mines city, in direction of Blanzy town, department of Saône-et-Loire (71), France. The age, depositional conditions, and stratigraphy are also summarized in Charbonnier et al. (2008). This quarry was located between the quarries of La Sorme and St Francois, all in activity between 1975 and 1980, opened for coal extraction by the French company \"les Houillères de Blanzy\".","environment":"deltaic indet.","primary_reference":"J. Myskowiak, J. M. Pouillon, and A. Nel. 2015. The oldest record of the grylloblattodean family Euryptilonidae discovered in the Late Carboniferous of France. Comptes Rendus Palevol 14:1-4","phylum":"Arthropoda","phylum_no":"18891","class":"Insecta","class_no":"56637","order":"Eoblattida","order_no":"200469","family":"Euryptilonidae","family_no":"175641","genus":"Montceaupterum","genus_no":"311424"},
