{"occurrence_no":"1305708","record_type":"occ","collection_no":"174767","identified_name":"Toucasiella gerardi","identified_rank":"species","accepted_name":"Toucasiella gerardi","accepted_rank":"species","accepted_no":"332533","early_interval":"Late Tithonian","max_ma":145.06,"min_ma":143.1,"reference_no":"57138","lng":"5.559500","lat":"44.541500","cc":"FR","latlng_basis":"estimated from map","latlng_precision":"4","geogscale":"small collection","geogcomments":"The locality lies in the cliffed upper valley of the River Drôme, in pine forest (Long 5°33'33\"E, Lat 44°32'32\"N) off the local road (D306) from Die to Valdrôme. It comprises a low mural section, 200 m-long, along a single track road on the north-west side of a precipitous gorge, the Ravin de Fournet. The section extends around the slope from an altitude of 928 m to a little above 1000 m.","environment":"carbonate indet.","primary_reference":"C. Frau, L. G. Bulot, and W. A. P. Wimbledon. 2015. Upper Tithonian Himalayitidae Spath, 1925 (Perisphinctoidea, Ammonitina) from Le Chouet (Drôme, France): implications for the systematics. Geologica Carpathica 66:117-132","phylum":"Mollusca","phylum_no":"7805","class":"Cephalopoda","class_no":"12315","order":"Ammonitida","order_no":"84931","family":"Himalayitidae","family_no":"132892","genus":"Toucasiella","genus_no":"332532"},
